      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"color-chains-and-conjugation\">Color chains and conjugation</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><a href=\"/\">Browse all notebooks</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"/?file=hep/qcd_gluons.py\">Quark annihilation into gluons</a></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Build SU(3) color generators using Spenso's existing tensor constructors.\nContracted fundamental indices can be collected into compact chains or traces.\nConjugation gives the same result before and after this collection.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">For Hermitian generators, conjugating <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||((T^a T^b)_{ij}||)</marimo-tex> gives\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||((T^b T^a)_{ji}||)</marimo-tex>. The order and endpoints both reverse. The trace of three\ngenerators can be complex, so its order must also reverse under conjugation.\nThese rules belong to shared Idenso algebra and also apply through\n<code>dirac_adjoint</code> when a larger expression contains fermion chains.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
